* rt_user.cal: run short user programs from a test in monitor mode.
* Include after rt_direct.cal.  The test must define
*
*     UPKG       word address of the user exchange package (a multiple of 20)
*
* and for each user program a word with its entry, UP1 being its label:
*
*     KP1      CON     UP1*T$P2_24
*
* UGO KP1 writes a fresh package at UPKG (P from KP1, base address 0, the
* largest limit address, monitor mode off, A2 = U$A2, everything else of
* words 0 to 3 zero, exchange address back to UPKG) and exchanges to it.
* The test goes on behind the UGO when the program exits or is
* interrupted; UPKG then holds the program's package.  Clobbers nothing of
* the test's: the exchange restores its A and S registers.
*
* UFLAG Sr leaves the F register of that package in Sr.
*
U$A2     =       D'3000                  ; A2 of every user program
         MACRO   UGO %KP
         U$S7,0  S7
         U$A7,0  A7
         S7      %KP,0
         UPKG,0  S7
         S7      0
         UPKG+1,0 S7
         S7      U$W2,0
         UPKG+2,0 S7
         S7      U$W3,0
         UPKG+3,0 S7
         A7      UPKG
         XA      A7
         S7      U$S7,0
         A7      U$A7,0
         EX
         ENDM
         MACRO   UFLAG %REG
         %REG    UPKG+3,0
         %REG    %REG<D'31               ; F is bits 31 to 39 from the left
         %REG    %REG>D'55
         ENDM
         MACRO   UDATA
U$S7     CON     0
U$A7     CON     0
U$W2     CON     T$LAMAX*T$P2_28+U$A2
U$W3     CON     UPKG/20*T$P2_40
         ENDM
